[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"Julia entry points when you embed DistSSHQueue. Day-to-day work stays on the CLI (julia --project=. -m DistSSHQueue …); see Home. The longer guide is the DistSSHKit manual. REPL help also works (?DistSSHQueue.submit!).\n\nSubmitters using DistSSHQueue. Queue-host code using DistSSHKit. Job files for go / ride still do not call DistSSHKit.\n\nPrefer the CLI. From a client: qhost:HOST on the command line (not --hosts). DISTSSHQUEUE_HOST alone does not hop. CLI submit uses follow_config; library submit! uses Queue(; allowed=…) unless follow_config=true. Config: ~/.distsshqueue/config.toml.\n\nusing DistSSHQueue\n\nq = Queue(; store=default_store_path(), follow_config=true)\nid = submit!(q, \"SCRIPT.jl\", \"child:host1:4\"; kind=:go)\ncancel!(q, id)\nserve!(q)","title":"API"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Types","page":"API","text":"Job persists the artifact-related fields used by cancel and fetch. Their ownership and fallback order are described in Artifacts and paths.","title":"Types"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Enqueue-and-cancel","page":"API","text":"","title":"Enqueue and cancel"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Table","page":"API","text":"","title":"Table"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#serve","page":"API","text":"","title":"serve"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Paths","page":"API","text":"default_store_path() is ~/.distsshqueue/jobs.toml. serve calls DistSSHKit execute!(…; detached=true, job_id=…).","title":"Paths"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.DistSSHQueue","page":"API","text":"DistSSHQueue — FIFO serve for DistSSHKit (go / ride / drive).\n\nPackage entry: exports, includes, main (@main on Julia 1.13+). FIFO: src/DistSSHQueue/. Client CLI: src/client/. Queue host CLI: src/qhost/. serve runs DistSSHKit execute!(...; detached=true). --project=<queue-env> loads this package; the Kit project is job_project(). Config: ~/.distsshqueue/config.toml.\n\nConcept: docs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.DistSSHQueue"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.Queue","page":"API","text":"FIFO table: one DistSSHKit job at a time. Placement tokens are Kit's, not a Queue ceiling.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.Queue"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.Job","page":"API","text":"One table row. hosts are DistSSHKit placement tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). kwargs is an opaque bag for DistSSHKit execute! (project is the Kit project).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.Job"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.submit!","page":"API","text":"Enqueue. kind is a DistSSHKit execute! kind (:go, :ride, :drive).\n\nhosts must be DistSSHKit 0.4 placement tokens (parent[:N] / child:NAME[:N]). Missing project uses job_project() (cwd / DISTRIBUTED_PROJECT_ROOT), not the serve env (enable --queue-env / Julia --project= that loaded Queue). Same verb as CLI submit.\n\nq.allowed is the inventory (Queue(; allowed=…)), names plus optional max :N. It does not read config.toml. CLI submit uses Queue(; follow_config=true) so each enqueue re-reads hosts without restarting serve. step! does not drop :queued rows when a name is later removed, and does not stop a Kit job that is already :running.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.submit!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.cancel!","page":"API","text":"Cancel :queued, or :running via DistSSHKit terminate_run! when the Kit sidecar dir is known.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.cancel!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.jobs","page":"API","text":"Copy of the table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.jobs"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.job","page":"API","text":"Copy of one row. id may be a unique prefix of the stored UUID.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.job"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.load!","page":"API","text":"Load store (stale :running → :failed).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.load!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.step!","page":"API","text":"Start the FIFO head if nothing is :running. At most one Kit job.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.step!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.serve!","page":"API","text":"Load store (stale :running → :failed), then step! until interrupt. Ctrl-C stops serve, not Kit.\n\nA second serve on the same store prints Already running and returns.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.serve!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#DistSSHQueue.job_project","page":"API","text":"Kit project: DISTRIBUTED_PROJECT_ROOT, else the Project.toml above cwd, else cwd.\n\nNot the Julia --project= that loaded DistSSHQueue.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DistSSHQueue.job_project"},{"category":"section","location":"assets/README/#Logo-and-social-preview-assets","page":"Logo & social-preview assets","text":"The mark is original geometry (no Julia dots). MIT, same as the package.\n\nThere is no SMIL / GIF bake. The source is logo/draw.jl with a pinned Luxor env (logo/Project.toml + logo/Manifest.toml). Do not Pkg.add Luxor into the package or docs project.\n\nassets/\n  custom.css\n  README.md\n  .raster-stamp-png     after local `--png` (CI freshness)\n  favicon.svg / favicon-dark.svg / favicon.ico   tab icon (plum Q; light + dark)\n  logo.svg              Documenter light (copy of logo/logo-static.svg)\n  logo-dark.svg         Documenter dark (copy of logo/logo-dark-static.svg)\n  logo/\n    Project.toml        Luxor pin\n    Manifest.toml\n    draw.jl             source (logo + social SVG)\n    logo-static.svg     README light (`<picture>` source)\n    logo-dark-static.svg\n    logo-static.png     local `--png`; README / JuliaHub fallback\n    logo-dark-static.png\n  social/\n    social-preview-static.svg\n    social-preview-static.png   GitHub OG 1280×640 (`--png`)\n\nDocumenter only discovers logo.svg / logo-dark.svg at this directory’s top level. Do not edit those copies by hand.\n\nGitHub README / README.ja use <picture> plus prefers-color-scheme for the footer logos. Dark / light source are the transparent SVGs. The fallback img is logo-static.png (paper background). JuliaHub strips or ignores <picture> / prefers-color-scheme (a transparent light SVG vanishes on a dark page). Absolute raw.githubusercontent.com/…/main/docs/src/assets/… so the files load.\n\nUpload social/social-preview-static.png under GitHub → Settings → Social preview.\n\njulia --project=docs/src/assets/logo -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'\njulia --project=docs/src/assets/logo docs/src/assets/logo/draw.jl\njulia --project=docs/src/assets/logo docs/src/assets/logo/draw.jl --png   # rasters\n\nCI (.github/workflows/assets-draw.yml) re-runs the SVG draw when this tree changes and fails if SVG outputs drift, or if PNG/ICO look older than their sources in git history (commit time of the raster, or .raster-stamp-png after a complete --png). Draw --png locally before committing rasters (CI does not render them).\n\nNeeds Luxor 4.5 via the pin above, not a global ] add.","title":"Logo & social-preview assets"},{"category":"section","location":"#DistSSHQueue.jl","page":"Home","text":"Leave jobs on a machine that stays on. They run one at a time. You can submit a job, check its status, fetch a finished leaf, and cancel. Supported on macOS, Linux, and WSL2 Ubuntu (not native Windows).\n\nThe longer guide is the DistSSHKit manual.","title":"DistSSHQueue.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Install","page":"Home","text":"pkg> add DistSSHQueue\n\nJulia 1.13+. The machine that stays on needs ssh and rsync. Git deploys also need git.","title":"Install"},{"category":"section","location":"#Commands","page":"Home","text":"The command is julia -m DistSSHQueue.\n\njulia -m DistSSHQueue qhost:HOST submit go SCRIPT.jl\njulia -m DistSSHQueue status\njulia -m DistSSHQueue fetch ID\n\nusing DistSSHQueue\nq = Queue(; store=default_store_path(), follow_config=true)\nid = submit!(q, \"SCRIPT.jl\", \"child:host1:4\"; kind=:go)","title":"Commands"}]
